# CI/CD (GitHub Actions)

See [docs/technical/infra/cicd.md](../../docs/technical/infra/cicd.md) for setup checklist and ADO mapping.

## Secrets vs variables

**Use GitHub variables (`vars.*`)** for non-sensitive configuration: resource names, public usernames, subscription IDs, client IDs, tenant IDs, image repository names passed as workflow inputs.

**Use GitHub secrets (`secrets.*`)** only for credentials: tokens, passwords, deployment keys (Docker Hub token, SWA deploy token, etc.).

Reusable workflows:

- Pass non-secrets via `workflow_call` **inputs** or read **`vars`** in the called workflow (e.g. `vars.DOCKERHUB_USERNAME` at repo level; environment-scoped vars on jobs with `environment: test`).
- Pass credentials via `workflow_call` **secrets** or `secrets: inherit` — repository secrets are **not** available in a called workflow unless inherited or passed explicitly. Never put secrets in `with:` inputs.

## Naming convention

Use **UPPER_SNAKE_CASE**. Prefer descriptive segments over putting a vague env token at the **start** of the name. For the **target env** suffix, use three-letter acronyms only: **`STG`** (legacy staging / GitHub `test`), **`DEV`** (development), **`PRD`** (production). Never use **`PROD`** — see [`.cursor/rules/env-acronyms.mdc`](env-acronyms.mdc).

**Azure and other cloud resources** (variables and secrets):

```
[SERVICEPROVIDER]_[SERVICETYPE]_[WORKLOADNAME]_[DESCRIPTION]_[TARGETENV]
```

| Segment | Meaning | Examples |
|---------|---------|----------|
| Service provider | Vendor / platform | `AZURE`, `DOCKERHUB` |
| Service type | Azure resource or product | `WEBAPP`, `FUNCTIONAPP`, `STATICWEBAPP`, `ENTRA`, `SUBSCRIPTION` |
| Workload name | Monorepo app or role | `API`, `FUNCTIONS`, `WEB`, `APP`, `OIDC`, `DEPLOY` |
| Description | What the value holds | `RESOURCENAME`, `DEPLOYTOKEN`, `CLIENTID`, `SUBSCRIPTIONID` |
| Target env | Stage suffix (three letters) | `STG` (GitHub `test`), `DEV` (development), `PRD` (production — never `PROD`) |

Examples:

| Kind | Name |
|------|------|
| Variable | `AZURE_WEBAPP_API_RESOURCENAME_STG` |
| Variable | `AZURE_FUNCTIONAPP_FUNCTIONS_RESOURCENAME_STG` |
| Variable | `AZURE_ENTRA_OIDC_CLIENTID_STG` |
| Secret | `AZURE_STATICWEBAPP_WEB_DEPLOYTOKEN_STG` |
| Secret | `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN` |

**Third-party accounts** that are not environment-specific may use a shorter `[PROVIDER]_[DESCRIPTION]` form (no target env suffix):

| Kind | Name |
|------|------|
| Variable | `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME` |
| Secret | `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN` |

Store environment-specific Azure values on the matching GitHub Environment (`development` → `*_DEV`, `production` → `*_PRD`). New-stack OIDC: `AZURE_ENTRA_OIDC_CLIENTID_SUBSCRIPTION` (subscription foundation only), `AZURE_ENTRA_OIDC_CLIENTID_WORKLOAD_<PART>` (that part’s infra and Src CD), shared `AZURE_ENTRA_OIDC_TENANTID` and `AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_DEPLOY_SUBSCRIPTIONID`.

## Layout

- `*-src-ci.yml` — build/test app source on pull requests **into `main`** (path-filtered)
- `*-src-cd.yml` — app source deploy on push to `main`; Environments `development` then gated `production`
- `*-infra-cd.yml` — Bicep at subscription or RG scope (`infra/bicep/<part>`). Subscription CD registers `resourceProvidersToRegister` from [`main.shared.bicepparam`](../../infra/bicep/subscription/main.shared.bicepparam) before deploy (workload SPs cannot).
- `reusable-src-*.yml` — app source deploy and Docker push templates
- `reusable-infra-*.yml` — Bicep deploy templates (subscription or resource group)
- Reusable workflows live at `.github/workflows/` top level; accept `environment` input (`development` \| `production`)
- Docker Hub tags for `development`: `latest-dev` and `{run_id}-dev` (never overwrite release `latest` / `{run_id}`)

## Agent access to GitHub

Configure GitHub MCP for Actions triage and PR creation — see [docs/technical/infra/github-mcp-setup.md](../../docs/technical/infra/github-mcp-setup.md). PAT needs **Pull requests: Read and write**; omit `X-MCP-Readonly` in `.cursor/mcp.json`.
